{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "primary_impacted_system",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "rationale": "Categorizing the affected system (wifi, vpn, database, etc.) gives a clean grouping axis for analyzing operational burdens. Values are well-grounded in short_description text. The 'network' inference for 'Printing issues' is a mild stretch but defensible."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_severity_indicator",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "rationale": "Classifying incidents as access_failure, service_unavailable, degraded, or config_error adds a genuine severity/type axis useful for the burden query. Mappings like 'Cannot connect' -> access_failure and 'Printing issues' -> service_degraded are reasonable readings of the text."
    },
    {
      "name": "scope_of_impact",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "rationale": "Scope (individual vs enterprise_wide) is analytically valuable for gauging operational burden. However the source text rarely states scope explicitly; e.g. 'Unable to connect to the office VPN' is labeled individual_user with no textual basis. Many labels appear to be assumptions the text does not directly support, though 'individual_user' as a default is a plausible weak inference."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_complexity_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "rationale": "Resolution complexity is a useful modeling axis. But short_descriptions describe the problem, not the fix, so labels like 'routine_access_restore' or 'infrastructure_intervention' are largely inferred/invented; nothing in 'Printing issues in office' warrants asserting 'infrastructure_intervention'. Groundedness is weak."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.86,
  "source_groundedness": 0.68,
  "rationale": "All four columns provide distinct, non-redundant axes (system, severity type, scope, resolution complexity) directly relevant to characterizing operational burdens, so analytical usefulness is high across the board. Groundedness varies: primary_impacted_system and issue_severity_indicator are sound readings of the description text, but scope_of_impact and especially resolution_complexity_signal assert facts (impact breadth, remediation effort) that the terse short_descriptions do not actually state, indicating some unwarranted inference."
}

